{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110901","id":2861320853,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6qjEqV","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110901","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110901.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110901.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110901","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110901/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110901/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110901/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/405651f6b56e869d5ce6c2d70eba8aacf8266145","number":110901,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Make `RD::texture_create` take a `Span<Span<uint8_t>>` to avoid needless allocations.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The API `RD::texture_create` currently necessitates allocation (often multiple) for calls.\r\nHowever, it only reads from the given arguments, so most of the time, no allocation should be necessary. This PR avoids allocation by using `Span` for the arguments instead.\r\n\r\nIn the end, `to_byte_array` was a code smell, and all of its users ended up copying data unnecessarily. To avoid this pattern in the future, I delete it from `LocalVector`, and discourage its use internally in `Vector`.\r\n\r\nNote: This is the first use of `FixedVector`, which is pending a fix: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106997\r\n\r\n## Caveats\r\n\r\nThe proposed API is just a bit weird when you think about it. We should discuss if it should be merged in the current state.\r\n\r\nFor one, some callers currently call `Image::get_data()` to gather each image's data into some list. If we simply used `get_data().span()`, the callee would be allowed to copy their data before return, the data would be deallocated after the call, and the `Span` created from it would be invalid. While this is not currently the case, the current API allows for it. To avoid this situation, I introduce `get_data_span()` to `Image`, to force it to return a `Span` to its own owned data. The new API could be used in other situations where a quick view into the data is needed.\r\n\r\nAnother weird point is that the new API can potentially _cause_ situations where additional allocations are needed:\r\nIf you have a `Vector<Vector<uint8_t>>` already, for whatever reason, this change will create the need to allocate for a `Vector<Span<uint8_t>>` instead.\r\nHowever, this does not happen in the codebase. There are basically just two situations:\r\n\r\n- The caller passes a known number of images (1 to 6), and this can be statically allocated.\r\n- The caller passes an unknown number of images as e.g. `TypedArray<PackedByteArray>` (aka `Vector<Variant>`), and conversions are needed anyway. The conversion to `LocalVector<Span<uint8_t>>` is cheaper than the previous one to `Vector<Vector<uint8_t>>`.\r\n\r\nFor both of these situations, no allocations are needed.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n`RenderingDevice::texture_create` sometimes adds more textures to the given ones. While it would be possible to implement this without many additional allocations, I just do it the same way the current implementation handles it and copy the given data if need be. It looks a little more complicated, but it's more performant than the previous implementation.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4